 Monthly Management Reporting & Actual vs Budget Performance Analysis 
.
1️⃣ Business Problem
Senior management needed a monthly reporting pack to:
 • Compare Actual vs Budget performance
 • Identify cost overruns & revenue gaps
 • Highlight material variances
 • Understand departmental & monthly trends

Key question:
 👉 Where are we missing the budget, why is it happening, and what actions will improve profitability?

2️⃣ Project Objectives
• Create a single source of truth for Actual vs Budget
 • Identify top variance drivers
 • Analyze monthly trends & seasonality
 • Flag material & unfavorable performance
 • Deliver an dashboard

3️⃣ Data Understanding
• Period: 2023–2025
 • ~2,000 monthly transactions
 • Dimensions: Month, Department, Account
 • Measures: Actual, Budget, Variance, Variance %

4️⃣ Tools & Skills Used
Tools:
 • Excel (PivotTables, PivotCharts, KPI cards, slicers)
Skills:
 • Financial reporting
 • Budget vs Actual analysis
 • KPI tracking
 • Trend & MoM analysis
 • Business storytelling 

5️⃣ Data Cleaning 
• Standardized department & account names
 • Separated Revenue vs Expense accounts
 • Applied consistent sign convention
 • Created calculated fields:
 – Variance
 – Variance %
 – Material flag
 – Performance classification
➡️ Ensured accurate aggregation and reliable insights

6️⃣ EDA
• Expenses consumed a disproportionate share of revenue
 • Finance & Operations emerged as largest cost centers
 • Clear seasonality with strong peaks (March, May, December)
 • Weak performance in mid-year months revealed planning gaps

7️⃣ Actual vs Budget Analysis (Core Insight)
• Revenue missed budget by ~80%
 • Expenses exceeded budget by ~390%
 • Resulting net profit gap ≈ $6M
➡️ Performance shortfall driven by both revenue underachievement and cost overruns

8️⃣ Variance Driver Analysis
• Sales & IT contributed over 50% of unfavorable variance
 • All departments showed material unfavorable variances
 • Over 60% of transactions were unfavorable vs plan
➡️ Indicates a systemic execution issue, not isolated exceptions

9️⃣ Month-over-Month Trends
• High volatility across months
 • Sharp drops during late summer periods
 • Limited smoothing or forecast adjustment
➡️ Signals weak forecasting discipline and reactive spending

🔟 Dashboard 
• KPI cards: Actual, Budget, Variance, Variance %
 • Visuals: Actual vs Budget, top variance drivers, monthly trends
 • Slicers: Month, Department, Account, Material flag
➡️ Enables fast executive review and drill-down decisions

1️⃣1️⃣ Business Impact
Current state:
 • Net profit gap: ~$6M
 • Expense overspend: ~390%
 • Unfavorable transactions: ~61%
Improvement scenario:
 • 10% cost reduction in Sales & IT
 • 15% revenue realization improvement
 • Monthly variance governance
➡️ Estimated 20–25% net profit improvement

1️⃣2️⃣ Recommendations
 • Tighten Sales & IT cost controls
 • Enforce monthly budget variance reviews
 • Improve revenue tracking by channel
 • Use MoM trends to refine forecasts
